      \"claim_id\": \"M-002\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The Nimbrel Probe stream name is what seperates one instrumented process from the next.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source B explicitly states that the stream name separates one instrumented process from another, matching the claim exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-003\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The stream name cant contain arbitrary symbols as documented\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A directly states that the stream name cannot contain arbitrary symbols, matching the claim with identical meaning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-004\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Stream name containing a . (dot) for exampe` checkout.web` along with a number of other symbols are refused by Nimbrel Probe\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source B explicitly states that stream names containing a dot (such as checkout.web) and other symbols are refused by Nimbrel Probe.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-005\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Stream names are validated against ^[A-Za-z0-9 -]+$ before the agent registers.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A states that stream names are validated against a pattern before the agent registers, directly supporting the claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-006\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Only letters, digits, spaces and hyphens are accepted\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_b.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source B explicitly lists the exact characters accepted for stream names, directly matching the claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-007\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"or the agent refuses to start.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A states that invalid stream names cause the agent to refuse to start, directly supporting the claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-008\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Stream names are validated against ^[A-Za-z0-9 -]+$ before the agent registers.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A provides the exact regex pattern and timing of validation that the claim states.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"one customer wanted the stream name left exactly as it stood\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A directly states that one customer wanted to keep the stream name exactly as it stood.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"that string was the product name in use everywhere in the org\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A states the stream name string was the product name in use throughout the organization, matching the claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and their reporting keyed of it when\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A indicates that customer reporting depended on the stream name, using the phrase 'reporting keyed of it'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Rename the stream to drop the unsupported symbols so the Nimbrel Probe agent will register\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A provides this as a solution, stating that renaming the stream enables the agent to register.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"M-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"carry the orignal name along as a global tag, so at least each trace keeps a link between the real name and the renamed one\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"source_a.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Source A describes using a global tag to maintain a link between original and renamed stream names in traces.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":15732,"type":"result","duration_ms":25037,"uuid":"40d1c768-131e-4c3c-bd9d-6a381b7a8462","ttft_stream_ms":987,"time_to_request_ms":183,"first_content_frame_ms":988,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
